  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed ground floor extension and proposed cycle store, by reason of their excessive combined ground coverage would result in an overdevelopment of the plot, unduly limiting open space provision within the rear garden and resulting in an uncharacteristically small rear garden that would appear unduly at odds with the established pattern of rear gardens within the locality. The proposed development would thereby be contrary to Policies; D3 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Core Strategy (2010), DMD 6, DMD 11 and DMD 37 of the Development Management Document (2014) as well as the high quality design aspiration set out within the NPPF (2026).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of Bedrooms 2, 3 and 6's inadequate widths and excessively narrow layouts would give rise to substandard and inappropriate accommodation, incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers of these particular bedrooms. Furthermore, the proposed development, by reason of its poor provision of outlook to Bedroom 2, would further compound impact in respect to occupants of Bedroom 2, providing a poor standard of accommodation. The proposed development would thereby be contrary to Policies; D3 and D6 of the London Plan, CP 4 and CP 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD 5, DMD 6, and DMD 8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), in addition to the high-quality design aspirations set out within the NPPF (2026).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of its failure to provide adequately sized and adequately configured external amenity space for occupants of the HMO would give rise to substandard and inappropriate accommodation, incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers. The proposed development would thereby be contrary to Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), CP 4 and CP 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD 6, DMD 8, and DMD 9 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), in addition to the high-quality design aspirations set out within the NPPF (2026).",
    "In the absence of a car parking survey examining on-street car parking capacity along this part of Alma Road and surrounding roads, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the proposed HMO, as a result of any potential uplift in overall occupation would not result in an undue increase in on-street car parking pressure within the locality. The proposed development would thereby be contrary to Policies; T2 and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021), CP24 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD 45 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) in addition to the NPPF (2026)."
  ]
}